-- The DEFINING module.  Two wrappers, both exported ABSTRACTLY (plain `export`,
-- constructors PRIVATE) — the ordinary way a library ships a wrapper type, and the
-- shape that made #2110's fix invisible across a module boundary before the
-- `deAtomsBefore` seed chain existed.
--
--   * `Slot` RE-SUPPLIES the atom: every occurrence of `e` in its fields sits under
--     a row that already carries <Stdout>, so `Slot <>` still unfolds to a
--     <Stdout>-performing field and a relay INTO it is honest.
--   * `Bare` SWALLOWS it: `e` occurs alone, so `Bare <>` hands back a pure-typed
--     function that prints.  A relay into it is the laundering shape.
--
-- The discriminator is per-DECLARATION, so both must cross the boundary or neither
-- proves anything: a seed that published nothing would reject BOTH in the entry,
-- and a seed that published everything unconditionally would accept both.
export data Slot e = Slot (Unit -> <Stdout | e> Unit)

export data Bare e = Bare (Unit -> <e> Unit)

export mkSlot : (Unit -> <Stdout | e> Unit) -> Slot e
mkSlot f = Slot f

export mkBare : (Unit -> <e> Unit) -> Bare e
mkBare f = Bare f
